=== program ===
{
 "title": "The hypothesis program, read out",
 "updated": "Last updated 2026-09-08 · thirty records and eleven folds under data/proving-ground · five refutations, one frozen promotion, one offline fold",
 "summary": "Two days of frozen paired experiments and offline folds on the operator’s subscription over the proving-ground bench. The noise floor is one flip in sixteen, so a delta has to be three flips wide before it says anything; the arms of an experiment still run one after the other, so an arm is confounded with its hour.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "mark": "refuted",
   "claim": "The harness loop loses to the product loop",
   "detail": "Sealed and capped at tier 5: 15 of 16 against 14, delta −0.0625, [−0.125, 0], inconclusive — one flip, inside the noise floor. The harness loop was faster in 15 of 16 pairs and 3.4 times cheaper in billed tokens, and both product misses breached a cap after one attempt. What the harness adds is the record, the seal, and caps that hold."
  },
  {
   "mark": "refuted",
   "claim": "A smaller model is as good on these tasks",
   "detail": "At tier 5 the three product models order strictly on every cell: haiku 1 of 16, sonnet 13 and 14, opus 16 of 16. The tier-3 reading that all three are level (18 of 18 each) was saturation; a bench that saturates cannot rank."
  },
  {
   "mark": "refuted",
   "claim": "A cheap-first cascade saves money",
   "detail": "Because the models order strictly per cell, the oracle that picks the cheapest certifying model is opus alone, and so is the strong-first cascade. Sonnet-then-opus costs 2.8 times the output tokens and 2.0 times the time; cheap-first over all three, 6.6 and 5.0 times. Nothing in the stamp tells a hard cell apart before a model runs."
  },
  {
   "mark": "refuted",
   "claim": "Attempts do not matter",
   "detail": "A three-rung ladder against a one-rung ladder of the same model: 15 of 16 against 9, delta −0.375, [−0.5625, −0.1875], reject for the cap of one. The first frozen verdict about a mechanism of the harness rather than a model. Half the delta is the later attempts; half is first-attempt variation the loop absorbs."
  },
  {
   "mark": "refuted",
   "claim": "Knowledge helps by being present",
   "detail": "Refuted from both sides. A catalog the tasks do not call for is never opened and costs wall time. Three skills they do call for are read in every cell, all three, and add no certificate: 13 of 16 against 14, 13, 15, and 15 in four sealed runs of the same model, four folds that never rise above zero."
  },
  {
   "mark": "supported",
   "claim": "opus over sonnet at tier 5",
   "detail": "16 of 16 against 13, delta 0.1875, [0.125, 0.25], promote: the only promotion-level verdict from a frozen pair, opus first-attempt on every cell and cheaper on every measure. It ranks a model tier, not the harness."
  },
  {
   "mark": "supported",
   "claim": "A fresh child per rung beats keeping the cheap model’s transcript",
   "detail": "14 of 16 against 11, 0.1875, [0.0625, 0.3125], promote by the fold’s thresholds, three flips all one way and all on the hardest tasks. An offline fold of arms that ran an hour apart and were never frozen together, so it is evidence, not a promotion; the frozen pair is queued."
